  "$comment": "Implementations additionally enforce <=16384 UTF-8 bytes, exact Int/Long numeric types, newest-first nondecreasing ages and row.share <= snapshot.share. Ages and counts saturate; see PROTOCOL_V1.md. Optional details additionally require strictly decreasing local attempt ordinals, share <= snapshot.share, sampleAgeMs <= ageMs, keyFramesEncoded <= framesEncoded when both known, and all measurements null when sampleAgeMs is null. Feedback counts are sender-received RTCP feedback. Details schema 2 additionally requires exact H264 capability opt-in, at most four encoded H264 observations per attempt, oldest-first nonincreasing observation ages <= attempt age, later observations declaredKey=true, width/height null or1..8192, unknown framing requires null presence, false presence requires complete inspection, and SPS metadata all null or all known with sps=true. Observation ages are independent of RTC stats sample age."
